   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: finding; i8962 p. 14, Line 10, Missing or incorrect SLCSP premium: \"If either of these two situations applies to you, or if you have reason to believe the Marketplace reported the wrong applicable SLCSP premium, you must determine the correct applicable SLCSP premium for every month\"; situation 1, \"If no APTC was paid ... column B ... may be wrong, left blank, or reported as -0-\"; p. 15, \"or if you have reason to believe the Marketplace reported the wrong applicable SLCSP premium\". f1095a.b_wrong tests only b_blank and b_changed, so a no-APTC form or one the filer otherwise believes wrong, with Part III the same every month, is taken as uniform without f1095a.b_fixed_same, and f1095a.mo_b takes the corrected premium as one amount the same every month; a correct premium that differs by month cannot be entered, and line 10 is Yes where the instructions give No. The model is right. Fix: add a no-APTC / reason-to-believe question as a third limb of b_wrong (BUG-0634).",
